nd (like a sequence ♥5 ♣6 ♥7 ♣8 or a pair ♣10 ♥10), which could help my teammate.  \n\nAmong the low singles, ♣8 is slightly better than ♥7 because 8 is higher and still low enough to conserve high cards. Playing ♣8 now wins the trick, lets me lead next, and doesn’t waste my high singles or jokers.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nI choose ♣8 because:  \n- It beats ♠6 minimally, conserving high cards for later critical moments.  \n- It allows me to take the lead and possibly play a sequence (♥5 ♣6 ♥7 ♣8) next to reduce my hand.  \n- Passing might let the landlord win with a low single and gain control. Since my teammate played a low card, they likely want me to take over.  \n- The rocket should be saved for beating bombs or regaining control when the landlord tries to finish.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": ["♣8"]}'}
